third_party/voice/sources.json text eol=lf
# These are prompt texts embedded with include_str! and sent to the model verbatim,
# so their bytes must not depend on how the build host checked them out. Evidence:
# the windows lane of CI run 39371971338 printed a rendered <permissions instructions>
# fragment whose wrapper lines carry \n (Rust literals) while its template-derived
# section carries "\r\n# Escalation Requests\r\n\r\n..." - mixed line endings inside
# one string can only come from a CRLF checkout, and GitHub's windows runners default
# to core.autocrlf=true. A forced autocrlf=true checkout of the same file reproduces
# those bytes here, and the checked-out file is LF on a macOS host. No HEAD blob under
# these directories contains a CR, so pinning eol=lf changes nothing that is committed
# and only constrains the checkout. These five are the template directories that Rust
# actually embeds with include_str!; codex-rs/core/templates/** is not embedded anywhere
# and is deliberately left alone. That CRLF is not what turned
# spawn_agent_can_fork_parent_thread_history_with_sanitized_items red on the same lane:
# the same test passes here with every permissions template converted to CRLF.
codex-rs/prompts/templates/** text eol=lf
codex-rs/memories/write/templates/** text eol=lf
codex-rs/ext/goal/templates/** text eol=lf
codex-rs/ext/memories/templates/** text eol=lf
codex-rs/collaboration-mode-templates/templates/** text eol=lf
# Raw SSE recordings end with a blank line delimiting the final event.
codex-rs/live-tests/tests/fixtures/*/responses-sse-*.txt whitespace=-blank-at-eof
